Given a table of flights, extract the 2nd flight with the most duration between each pair of cities. Order the flights by the flight id ascending.
 
Note: For any cities X and Y, (source_location=X, destination_location=Y) and (source_location=Y, destination_location=X) are counted as the same pair of cities.
 
Note: If there are fewer than two flights between two cities, there is no 2nd longest flight.
 
 
id	destination_location	source_location	plane_id	flight_start	flight_end
1	Paris	Rome	1	2021-01-01 12:00:00	2021-01-01 14:00:00
2	Paris	Rome	2	2021-01-01 12:00:00	2021-01-01 14:10:00
3	Rome	Munich	3	2021-01-01 12:00:00	2021-01-01 13:30:00
4	Rome	Belgrade	4	2021-01-01 12:00:00	2021-01-01 13:25:00
5	Munich	Paris	5	2021-01-01 12:00:00	2021-01-01 13:35:00
6	Paris	Munich	6	2021-01-01 12:00:00	2021-01-01 13:30:00
7	Munich	Paris	7	2021-01-02 12:00:00	2021-01-02 13:25:00
8	Munich	Paris	8	2021-01-02 12:00:00	2021-01-02 13:20:00

