from pyspark.sql import functions as F
from pyspark.sql.window import Window

df1 = df.withColumn(
    "city_pair",
    F.concat_ws(
        "-",
        F.least("source_location", "destination_location"),
        F.greatest("source_location", "destination_location")
    )
)

w = Window.partitionBy("city_pair").orderBy(
    F.unix_timestamp("flight_end") - F.unix_timestamp("flight_start")
)

result = (
    df1.withColumn("rn", F.row_number().over(w.orderBy(
        F.desc(F.unix_timestamp("flight_end") - F.unix_timestamp("flight_start"))
    )))
    .filter("rn = 2")
    .orderBy("id")
)

result.show()



The key idea is:

Use least() and greatest() to make Paris-Rome and Rome-Paris the same pair.
Calculate flight duration.
Use row_number() ordered by duration descending.
Keep rn = 2 (the second longest flight).
Sort by id ascending.
